{"step_index":620,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T17:59:20Z","content":"**Updated to `gemini-3.6-flash` and deployed live to Surge!**\n\n---\n\n### What Was Updated:\n1. **Model Upgraded:** Both the **Vision AI Lead Sheet Parser** and the **AI SMS Copywriting Engine** are now updated to **`gemini-3.6-flash`**.\n2. **Resilient Multi-Model Fallbacks:** Added automatic tier fallbacks (`gemini-3.6-flash` $\\rightarrow$ `gemini-2.0-flash` $\\rightarrow$ `gemini-1.5-flash`) so the app adapts seamlessly across different Google AI Studio key tiers.\n3. **Compiled & Deployed Live:** Rebuilt and published directly to **[https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh](https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh)**.\n\n---\n\n### Test on Your Phone:\nSimply open **SnapDialer** on your iPhone (or refresh the page), snap your lead sheet, and it will process directly with Gemini 3.6 Flash!"}
{"step_index":621,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T18:03:46Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nthe app seems to be making individual lists for each lead added.  this would be okay if i were grabbing multiple leads from one sheet, but each photo i import represents only one lead...not multiple.  i think we need to abandon the whole 'list' philosophy and just recognize that we're working with a bunch of individual leads.  we can capture the date/time the entered the system, but maintaining entire separate lists with dates is not necessary\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-20T14:03:46-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":622,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T18:03:47Z","thinking":"**Defining the Core Workflow**\n\nOkay, I've got a handle on the user's workflow. It appears each imported photo represents a single FRS Report Card from ValuTeachers. That's a key piece of the puzzle and now I can start evaluating the impacts.\n\n\n**Reimagining the App Architecture**\n\nI'm now focusing on restructuring the app's core architecture. The redesign centers around a unified \"Educator Lead Hub,\" replacing the cumbersome list-based system. The home screen will become an Educator Lead Pipeline, displaying all leads in a single view with filtering and sorting capabilities. A dynamic top bar will give key stats at a glance.\n\n\n**Implementing New Functionality**\n\nI'm now integrating crucial features. There's a powerful search function by name, school, or room number, and date/time capture for added context. The power dialer queue is a priority, offering one-tap dialing and filtering by lead status. Streamlined \"Snap Sheet\" workflow saves leads with a single tap, bypassing list management. Direct lead actions are also being implemented for each card.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\db\\leadsRepository.ts","toolAction":"Viewing leadsRepository.ts","toolSummary":"View leadsRepository.ts"}}]}
